data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"The variance of component $i$ is $s_i^2/(n-1)$, with $s_i$ the singular values of the centred data. Divide each by the\ntotal variance of all columns, which is the sum of the column variances with divisor $n-1$. Accumulate the ratios\nwith a cumulative sum. The answer is the first index where the sum reaches the threshold, counted from one. Allow a\nmargin of $10^{-12}$ below the threshold, so that a tie in exact arithmetic is not lost to rounding."},"hints_note":null}

